  "notes": "FORMS:\n{開|かい} (open) + {封|ふう} (seal). Literally \"opening the seal.\"\n\nUSAGE:\nCommonly seen on product labels, food packaging, and in online shopping contexts. Used as a suru verb: {開封|かいふう}する (to open/unseal).\nProduct labels often say {開封|かいふう}{後|ご}はお{早|はや}めにお{召|め}し{上|あ}がりください (please consume promptly after opening). In e-commerce, {未開封|みかいふう} items can typically be returned, while {開封|かいふう}{済|ず}み items often cannot.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {開封|かいふう}{後|ご}: after opening\n- {開封|かいふう}{済|ず}み: already opened\n- {未開封|みかいふう}: unopened, still sealed\n- {開封|かいふう}{厳禁|げんきん}: do not open\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {封|ふう}をする / {封|ふう}をとじる: to seal (the opposite action)",
